# Evidence Records

Evidence records state:

- subject and exact version;
- observation time;
- method or command;
- environment and scope;
- result;
- limitations;
- related requirements, findings, decisions, tasks, and gates.

Do not create a passing evidence record before the check actually runs.
Evidence is immutable after recording except for a clearly labeled correction
or successor. Record command/tool version, source fingerprint or revision,
dirty/untracked/ignored scope, start/end time, environment, checks, result,
freshness rule, and limitations. Never include secret values.
